# Explicit State Machines

Any entity that changes state over time must have a documented state machine:

- Possible states are enumerated and finite
- Valid transitions are declared explicitly (from → to, trigger, permitted role)
- Invalid transitions raise domain exceptions — never fail silently
- Terminal states allow no further transitions

The state machine lives in the Domain layer. No outer layer decides the next state directly.

## Example Transition Declaration

| From      | To        | Trigger        | Permitted Role |
|-----------|-----------|----------------|----------------|
| `Draft`   | `Active`  | `Publish`      | `Admin`        |
| `Active`  | `Closed`  | `Close`        | `Admin`        |
